spans.s:
múñj-a, m. [resounding, rustling], 🞄reed-grass, sedge;
 sp. a kind of rush (Saccharum 🞄munja) from the fibres of which the 🞄Brāhmanʼs girdle is made;
 N. of various 🞄men.

muñja-keśa, a. having hair resembling 🞄reed-grass, ep. of Viṣṇu and Śiva;
 m. 🞄N.;
 -dhārin, a. holding muñja grass in oneʼs 🞄hand;
 -néjana, a. purified from reed-grass 🞄(RV.¹);
 -maya, a. (ī) consisting of muñja 🞄grass;
 -mekhalin, a. having a girdle of reed-grass, 🞄ep. of Viṣṇu and Śiva;
 -vāsas, a. 🞄having a garment of reed-grass, ep. of Śiva.
